# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Peter K. Eastman et al. (2023). SPICE, A Dataset of Drug-like Molecules and Peptides for Training Machine Learning Potentials.
#   Scientific Data. doi:10.1038/s41597-022-01882-6  arXiv:2209.10702v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2209.10702v2 (sha256 3a0ad22538cb2f79...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 15 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the SPICE data set (version 1; six subsets, 1,132,808
# conformations at the omegaB97M-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVPPD level) and the
# proof-of-concept Equivariant Transformer model trained on it (the best
# of an ensemble of five), with the one energy MAE the paper prints.

